1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,980
In August twenty nineteen,

2
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:04,300
a couple in Massachusetts began receiving things

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,400
that made no sense.

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:07,000
Live insects.

5
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:08,660
Threatening messages.

6
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:10,480
A bloody pig mask.

7
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:13,620
And eventually, people connected to the campaign

8
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,820
were watching them in person and trying

9
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,680
to put a G-P-S tracker on their

10
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:17,940
car.

11
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,420
At first glance, this sounds like an

12
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,760
internet stalking story.

13
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,940
But the people behind it were not

14
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,840
anonymous trolls.

15
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:27,040
They worked in, or with,

16
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:29,240
the security organization of eBay.

17
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:33,180
All seven former employees and contractors who

18
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:35,840
were federally prosecuted over the campaign later

19
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:36,640
pleaded guilty.

20
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:40,760
Years later, prosecutors filed criminal charges against

21
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:41,720
eBay itself.

22
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,860
The company entered a deferred prosecution agreement,

23
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:47,340
admitted a detailed factual account,

24
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:49,840
paid a three-million-dollar criminal penalty,

25
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,660
and accepted an independent compliance monitor.

26
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:54,880
And in July twenty twenty-six,

27
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,360
the civil case ended in an announced

28
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:01,640
settlement package worth fifty-five-point-seven million dollars.

29
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:03,600
But the strangest part is not what

30
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:04,720
arrived at the front door.

31
00:01:05,460 --> 00:01:06,920
It is how criticism of a company

32
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:09,720
became a security problem inside that company

33
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:12,480
and how the consequences kept growing long

34
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,980
after the harassment stopped.

35
00:01:14,680 --> 00:01:17,340
Ina and David Steiner ran EcommerceBytes,

36
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:21,260
an independent publication covering online commerce since

37
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:22,100
nineteen ninety-nine.

38
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,620
The scale mismatch was obvious:

39
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,520
an independent trade publication on one side,

40
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,480
a global marketplace on the other.

41
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,480
But the Steiners covered eBay's world closely

42
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:33,320
sellers,

43
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,140
marketplace rules, executive decisions,

44
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:38,380
and the complaints of people who depended

45
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:39,720
on platforms like eBay.

46
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:41,680
By spring twenty nineteen,

47
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:44,380
a later federal court record shows that

48
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:47,360
EcommerceBytes had become an increasing source of

49
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:50,020
frustration for people inside eBay's leadership.

50
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:52,660
The Steiners were not business rivals trying

51
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:53,800
to take eBay's customers.

52
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:57,200
They were publishers criticizing the company and

53
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,020
giving readers a place to criticize it

54
00:01:59,020 --> 00:01:59,260
too.

55
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,760
Companies face criticism every day.

56
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:04,200
The real question is how criticism from

57
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:07,720
two publishers became something people inside eBay's

58
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,260
security organization were expected to solve.

59
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,840
The internal messages are where the story

60
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,320
changes.

61
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,120
In April twenty nineteen,

62
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:19,840
Steve Wymer eBay's communications chief sent then-C-E-O

63
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:22,600
Devin Wenig a message about an Ina

64
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,460
Steiner article.

65
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:24,780
His words were:

66
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,920
We are going to crush this lady.

67
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,620
Weeks later, according to the federal court

68
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,400
record, Wenig told Wymer to take her

69
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:32,740
down.

70
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:34,760
And on August first,

71
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
another message from Wenig said that if

72
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,260
they were ever going to act,

73
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:39,860
now is the time.

74
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,800
Those words are dramatic.

75
00:02:42,420 --> 00:02:43,140
But they are not,

76
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:45,740
by themselves, proof that Wenig or any

77
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:48,060
other executive ordered the crimes that followed.

78
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,560
The later court record says Jim Baugh

79
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,140
the head of eBay security

80
00:02:52,780 --> 00:02:55,500
testified that Wenig never communicated directly with

81
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,460
him about the Steiners.

82
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,680
Wenig's relevant communications went through Wymer.

83
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,700
Still, inside the organization,

84
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,440
the language was escalating.

85
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,720
Wymer's messages to Baugh became increasingly ag

86
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:07,120
gressive,

87
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:09,800
including the phrase Whatever it takes.

88
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:13,120
Another executive relationship was pulling the issue

89
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,220
toward security too.

90
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:17,320
Wendy Jones Baugh's direct supervisor

91
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,700
told him, according to the court record,

92
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,020
to handle the issue off the radar

93
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:24,200
and said she did not want details.

94
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,340
That is not the same as a

95
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,200
finding that Jones knew what the security

96
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:29,480
team would later do.

97
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:30,780
But by this point,

98
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,580
criticism from two publishers was no longer

99
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:36,120
being discussed only as a communications problem.

100
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,300
It had entered the security chain.

101
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,420
Before the most notorious phase of the

102
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:44,720
campaign, members of Baugh's security operation had

103
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,140
already traveled to Massachusetts.

104
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,080
During an early trip,

105
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:51,840
security employee Brian Gilbert surveilled the Steiners

106
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,920
and spray-painted FidoMaster on their fence

107
00:03:55,740 --> 00:03:57,680
a username used by a commenter on

108
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,680
EcommerceBytes whom the security team believed was

109
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:01,820
connected to the Steiners.

110
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:04,760
Baugh later described the trip to Wymer

111
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:06,500
as a tap on the shoulder.

112
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:09,900
That moment matters because it shows how

113
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:12,140
the problem was being translated inside the

114
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:12,480
company.

115
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,260
At the top, there was anger about

116
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:15,720
criticism.

117
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:19,020
In the middle, increasingly forceful messages.

118
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,920
At the security level,

119
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:22,820
those messages were becoming action.

120
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:25,580
Then the process became more organized.

121
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:29,600
On August sixth, Baugh held meetings with

122
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:32,380
security-team members to plan an operation against

123
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,040
the Steiners.

124
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:36,800
The plan included unwanted deliveries and online

125
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:37,440
harassment.

126
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,820
The next day, Baugh met with Wymer.

127
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:43,080
And then the operation accelerated.

128
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,940
The Steiners began receiving threatening online messages

129
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:48,240
and disturbing deliveries.

130
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:52,200
The admitted record includes live insects and

131
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,200
a bloody pig mask.

132
00:04:54,220 --> 00:04:56,680
There were also Craigslist posts designed to

133
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,220
send strangers toward the Steiners and other

134
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,920
messages intended to frighten them.

135
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:03,680
The details are bizarre enough to make

136
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:05,340
the story feel almost unreal.

137
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:07,800
But the key point is that this

138
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,420
was organized.

139
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,640
People were planning activities,

140
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:12,300
traveling, communicating,

141
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:16,380
and using corporate-security personnel and resources around

142
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,820
a campaign directed at two private citizens.

143
00:05:19,880 --> 00:05:21,420
Then the line moved again.

144
00:05:22,540 --> 00:05:24,180
On August fifteenth, Baugh,

145
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:27,340
David Harville and Veronica Zea traveled to

146
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:28,140
the Steiners area.

147
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:30,660
According to the federal court record,

148
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:33,340
they attempted to install a G-P-S tracker

149
00:05:33,340 --> 00:05:34,420
on the Steiners vehicle.

150
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:37,480
They also surveilled and followed the couple.

151
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:40,360
The tracker was not established as successfully

152
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:41,040
installed.

153
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,700
But the attempt changed the nature of

154
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:44,100
the story.

155
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:47,160
This was no longer just anonymous online

156
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:49,320
harassment or disturbing deliveries.

157
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:52,520
It had become a physical surveillance operation.

158
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,200
And the next day,

159
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:55,800
the Steiners went to the police.

160
00:05:56,860 --> 00:05:59,837
Natick police began investigating on August sixteenth,

161
00:05:59,837 --> 00:06:00,580
twenty nineteen.

162
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:03,000
That should have ended the operation.

163
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:06,060
Instead, it created a second problem.

164
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:08,740
The first was what the security team

165
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:09,120
had done.

166
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:11,460
The second was what members of that

167
00:06:11,460 --> 00:06:14,300
team did once investigators started asking questions.

168
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:17,520
The record admitted by eBay and described

169
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:20,780
by federal prosecutors includes false statements,

170
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:22,460
deletion of digital evidence,

171
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,240
and falsified records.

172
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:27,640
A security organization that existed to reduce

173
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:30,120
risk had now created two kinds of

174
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:30,300
risk:

175
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:33,580
the operation itself, and the effort to

176
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,160
conceal it.

177
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:37,660
eBay began its own internal investigation days

178
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:38,140
later.

179
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,940
By the end of August,

180
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,560
several security employees had been placed on

181
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:42,780
leave.

182
00:06:43,760 --> 00:06:45,820
Over time, key members of the operation

183
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:47,440
were removed or terminated,

184
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,060
and one contractor's relationship ended.

185
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:53,000
But internal discipline was only the beginning.

186
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,800
Federal prosecutors were coming next.

187
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:57,820
Beginning in twenty twenty,

188
00:06:58,240 --> 00:07:01,300
federal prosecutors brought criminal cases against people

189
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:02,360
involved in the campaign.

190
00:07:03,480 --> 00:07:06,580
Eventually, all seven former eBay employees and

191
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:09,180
contractors who were prosecuted pleaded guilty.

192
00:07:10,420 --> 00:07:12,540
A guilty plea is not an allegation.

193
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:15,840
It establishes criminal guilt without a trial.

194
00:07:16,940 --> 00:07:19,600
Jim Baugh received fifty-seven months in prison.

195
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,820
David Harville received twenty-four months.

196
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:26,380
Other participants received combinations of prison,

197
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:29,880
probation, home confinement, and financial penalties.

198
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:32,220
By twenty twenty-four,

199
00:07:32,860 --> 00:07:35,480
the individual criminal cases had produced a

200
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:37,320
clear story of personal accountability.

201
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:39,240
And from a distance,

202
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:40,880
that can look like the ending.

203
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:44,080
eBay had removed key members of the

204
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:44,820
security operation.

205
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,160
The people who were federally prosecuted had

206
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:48,780
pleaded guilty.

207
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:52,820
But federal prosecutors eventually turned from the

208
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:55,560
individuals inside the company to the company

209
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:56,000
itself.

210
00:07:57,340 --> 00:07:58,880
In January twenty twenty-four,

211
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:02,940
prosecutors filed a six-count criminal Information against

212
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:03,160
eBay.

213
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,460
The counts included interstate stalking,

214
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,840
stalking through electronic communications,

215
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,280
witness tampering,

216
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:14,080
and destruction or falsification of records connected

217
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,500
to a federal investigation.

218
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:19,020
But eBay was not convicted on those

219
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:19,300
charges.

220
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,180
Instead, the company entered a deferred prosecution

221
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:23,880
agreement.

222
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:27,940
A deferred prosecution agreement works differently from

223
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:28,380
a conviction.

224
00:08:29,420 --> 00:08:30,760
The government files charges,

225
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:33,560
but prosecution is held back while the

226
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:35,980
company complies with negotiated conditions.

227
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:39,100
If the agreement is completed successfully,

228
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:41,840
the criminal case is intended to end

229
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:44,080
without a trial on those corporate charges.

230
00:08:45,140 --> 00:08:45,600
For eBay,

231
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:48,120
the agreement came with real consequences.

232
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:52,020
The company admitted a detailed factual account

233
00:08:52,020 --> 00:08:52,680
of the conduct.

234
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:56,140
It agreed to pay a three-million-dollar criminal

235
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:56,780
penalty.

236
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:00,260
And it accepted an independent compliance monitor

237
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:03,320
for three years, along with cooperation and

238
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,240
compliance obligations.

239
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:08,560
At that point, the legal consequences no

240
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,540
longer belonged only to individuals.

241
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:13,820
eBay itself had entered a federal criminal

242
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:15,980
resolution tied to the conduct.

243
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:19,600
But one major question was still unresolved.

244
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:23,300
How far up the organization could civil

245
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:25,860
responsibility for the campaign extend?

246
00:09:26,960 --> 00:09:29,300
That question was moving toward a jury.

247
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:33,020
The Steiners filed their federal civil case

248
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:34,500
in July twenty twenty-one.

249
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:38,600
Four years later, Judge Patti Saris issued

250
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,400
a major summary-judgment order.

251
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:43,760
At this stage, the key distinction is

252
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:44,020
simple:

253
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:47,180
allowing a claim to continue does not

254
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:49,240
mean a defendant has been found liable.

255
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,980
It means the issue can still be

256
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:53,080
decided by a jury.

257
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:56,600
And the court treated different defendants differently.

258
00:09:57,780 --> 00:10:01,480
A security contractor named P-F-C won summary

259
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,440
judgment on the claims against it.

260
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:07,420
But significant claims involving eBay and former

261
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:08,760
executives survived.

262
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:12,620
For Devin Wenig, the record included an

263
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:13,540
important limitation:

264
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:17,260
Baugh testified that Wenig had not communicated

265
00:10:17,260 --> 00:10:19,440
with him directly about the Steiners.

266
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,340
At the same time,

267
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:22,720
the judge held that,

268
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,860
viewing the evidence in the Steiners favor

269
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,740
as required at that stage,

270
00:10:27,420 --> 00:10:30,180
a jury could potentially find Wenig's encouragement

271
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:33,060
was a substantial factor in what followed.

272
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:35,940
Wenig disputed that interpretation.

273
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:39,380
His lawyers said he had no knowledge

274
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:42,460
of or involvement in the harassment campaign,

275
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:45,260
did not approve or authorize it,

276
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:48,120
and argued that his messages concerned a

277
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:50,940
public-relations response to the Steiners reporting.

278
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:54,380
For Steve Wymer, the court pointed to

279
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:57,260
a more extensive communication record and held

280
00:10:57,260 --> 00:10:59,780
that a reasonable jury could find he

281
00:10:59,780 --> 00:11:00,400
had induced,

282
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:03,820
encouraged or authorized tortious conduct.

283
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:07,200
Again, that was not a final finding

284
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:07,640
of liability.

285
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,040
And Wenig, Wymer and Wendy Jones were

286
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,260
not criminally charged over the campaign.

287
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:19,340
eBay's internal-investigation position also cut the other

288
00:11:19,340 --> 00:11:19,600
way:

289
00:11:20,420 --> 00:11:22,920
according to reporting on a company presentation,

290
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,500
its lawyers said they had found no

291
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:28,480
evidence that Wenig or Wymer directed the

292
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,060
criminal acts or knew those acts would

293
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:31,400
follow.

294
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,420
So by late twenty twenty-five,

295
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:38,040
the unresolved question was how far responsibility

296
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,960
extended above the people who had carried

297
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:42,280
out the security operation.

298
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,720
A jury was getting close to answering

299
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,080
that.

300
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,000
Then the case appeared to end.

301
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:52,680
On February twenty-fifth, twenty twenty-six,

302
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:55,540
just before trial, the parties reported a

303
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,520
settlement in principle.

304
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,560
The terms were not disclosed.

305
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:02,080
The case was conditionally dismissed while they

306
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,480
worked to finalize the agreement.

307
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:05,820
After years of criminal cases,

308
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:09,640
a corporate D-P-A, civil discovery and pretrial

309
00:12:09,640 --> 00:12:11,780
rulings, it looked like the final chapter.

310
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,820
Then the deal failed.

311
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:16,860
By June, the settlement had not been

312
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:17,140
finalized.

313
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,400
The civil case was reopened.

314
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,620
A new trial date was set for

315
00:12:21,620 --> 00:12:23,180
January twenty twenty-seven.

316
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:27,320
That put the unresolved civil-responsibility question back

317
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:27,880
on the table.

318
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:30,160
But before a jury could hear the

319
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,340
case, the parties reached another deal.

320
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:34,480
This one became the final settlement.

321
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,000
And this time, the numbers were public.

322
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:39,920
The final agreement was announced in late

323
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,360
July twenty twenty-six.

324
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:45,640
The total announced settlement package was fifty-five-point-seven

325
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,940
million dollars.

326
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:48,600
But that number has to be broken

327
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:48,940
apart.

328
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:52,520
It was not a fifty-five-point-seven-million-dollar judgment.

329
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:55,900
And it was not a fifty-five-point-seven-million-dollar payment

330
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:57,680
made only by eBay.

331
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,000
According to the announced terms,

332
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:03,560
forty-eight-point-seven million dollars was compensation to the

333
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,000
Steiners.

334
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:07,060
Another seven million dollars consisted of charitable

335
00:13:07,060 --> 00:13:07,640
commitments.

336
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:09,400
Of the direct compensation,

337
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:14,660
eBay's announced share was forty-six-point-one-five million dollars.

338
00:13:14,660 --> 00:13:16,180
Devin Wenig's was two million.

339
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,840
Wendy Jones's was five hundred thousand.

340
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,260
Steve Wymer's was fifty thousand.

341
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:24,860
Separately, eBay committed six million dollars to

342
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:25,920
nonprofit organizations,

343
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,880
and Wenig committed one million dollars to

344
00:13:28,880 --> 00:13:31,780
a First Amendment-focused charity in Ina Steiner's

345
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:32,020
name.

346
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:35,580
That is how the total reached fifty-five-point-seven

347
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:35,940
million.

348
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:38,580
And that number should not be combined

349
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:42,540
with eBay's separate three-million-dollar criminal penalty and

350
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:45,700
presented as a fifty-eight-point-seven-million-dollar award.

351
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:47,520
There was no such award.

352
00:13:48,320 --> 00:13:50,660
These were separate legal resolutions with different

353
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:51,220
purposes.

354
00:13:51,220 --> 00:13:54,440
One was a federal criminal resolution involving

355
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:55,080
the company.

356
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:57,640
The other was the final civil settlement

357
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:58,040
package.

358
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:00,480
The cost did not arrive in one

359
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,840
courtroom on one day.

360
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,700
It accumulated over years.

361
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,740
In its July twenty twenty-six statement,

362
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:09,700
eBay apologized to Ina and David Steiner.

363
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,920
The company called the conduct of the

364
00:14:11,920 --> 00:14:14,500
former employees wrong and reprehensible.

365
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:17,160
It also acknowledged what it described as

366
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,000
unprofessional communications involving Wenig,

367
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,280
Wymer and Jones.

368
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,700
But the settlement meant there would be

369
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:26,620
no jury verdict deciding the surviving civil-liability

370
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:29,060
questions against those former executives.

371
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,400
So the ending is not that a

372
00:14:31,400 --> 00:14:32,880
court answered every question.

373
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:34,060
It did not.

374
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,820
What the public record does show is

375
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:37,080
enough.

376
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:40,540
A small publication criticized a global marketplace.

377
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:42,340
Inside eBay,

378
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,720
that criticism generated escalating internal hostility.

379
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,700
The issue moved into corporate security.

380
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,800
Security personnel planned and carried out harassment

381
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:52,460
and surveillance.

382
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:54,740
When police began investigating,

383
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:57,020
the problem expanded into obstruction.

384
00:14:57,900 --> 00:15:00,400
Seven prosecuted participants pleaded guilty.

385
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:03,340
eBay itself later entered a federal deferred

386
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:06,460
prosecution agreement, admitted detailed facts,

387
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:08,980
paid a three-million-dollar criminal penalty,

388
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,140
and accepted an independent monitor.

389
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:14,460
Years of civil litigation then pushed unresolved

390
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:18,040
questions about responsibility higher into the organization.

391
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:21,080
The first twenty twenty-six settlement failed.

392
00:15:21,900 --> 00:15:23,460
The second ended the case with a

393
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:26,520
fifty-five-point-seven-million-dollar settlement package.

394
00:15:27,320 --> 00:15:28,540
There were personal costs:

395
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,740
guilty pleas and prison sentences.

396
00:15:31,660 --> 00:15:33,220
There were corporate legal costs:

397
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:34,360
federal charges,

398
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:35,440
a D-P-A,

399
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,400
a penalty, and monitoring.

400
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,360
And there were civil financial costs measured

401
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:42,180
i n tens of millions of dollars.

402
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,140
All of that grew out of a

403
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:46,600
problem every major company eventually faces:

404
00:15:47,460 --> 00:15:47,840
criticism.

405
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:50,480
The expensive decision was not that the

406
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:51,340
criticism existed.

407
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,860
It was what people inside the company

408
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:55,160
decided to do about it.

409
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,920
And that is what it cost.

